        },
        {
          "name": "dark-surface",
          "script": "dark-surface/check.py",
          "args": [],
          "timeout": 10,
          "isolate": null,
          "side_effect": "shadow-sink",
          "emits": true,
          "comment": "A6 wire-dormant-gates. dark-surface/check.py:13-14 already documents 'this is the mode the session-new _dispatch/manifest.json runs it under', but the entry was never actually added -- the GREEN-not-LIVE defect the gate itself exists to catch. stub-ledger/report.py:258 returns 0 on a completion-claim Stop turn to 'defer to dark-surface', so while this was unwired NEITHER gate fired on exactly the turns that matter. Shadow/observe-only by default (DARK_SURFACE_MODE=shadow), inject-only, never blocks, fail-open. side_effect is 'shadow-sink' not 'none' because it appends to ~/.agents/state/harness/shadow/shadow-<day>.jsonl (check.py:115-145); the neighbouring side_effect='none' checks write nothing. Opt-out: DARK_SURFACE=off or hooks/dark-surface/.disabled."
